107
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,830
out before I've had a fair chance to

108
00:04:19,840 --> 00:04:22,790
read it and respond. That kind of design

109
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:24,870
assumes speed and motor control that not

110
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:27,749
everyone has. There are also structural

111
00:04:27,759 --> 00:04:30,950
assumptions that focus will not matter,

112
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:32,870
that a custom control does not need a

113
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:35,430
proper role, that a drag gesture is fine

114
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:37,430
as the only way to do something, or that

115
00:04:37,440 --> 00:04:39,350
a user can easily recover if they press

116
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:41,990
the wrong thing. More generally,

117
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,670
software often assumes the user

118
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:45,110
interacts in the same way as the

119
00:04:45,120 --> 00:04:47,590
