1198
00:46:28,079 --> 00:46:29,829
build certain kinds of access tools

1199
00:46:29,839 --> 00:46:32,950
properly. Platform vendors decide what

1200
00:46:32,960 --> 00:46:36,470
is possible. If an API does not exist or

1201
00:46:36,480 --> 00:46:38,950
if it is unreliable, every assistive

1202
00:46:38,960 --> 00:46:40,790
technology developer has to work around

1203
00:46:40,800 --> 00:46:44,230
that limitation and users pay the price.

1204
00:46:44,240 --> 00:46:45,910
Vendors should make accessibility

1205
00:46:45,920 --> 00:46:48,309
features reliable across updates.

1206
00:46:48,319 --> 00:46:50,390
Provide stable ways to inspect UI

1207
00:46:50,400 --> 00:46:52,710
structure and perform user actions.

1208
00:46:52,720 --> 00:46:54,950
Avoid breaking assistive technology and

1209
00:46:54,960 --> 00:46:56,870
involve disabled users and specialist

1210
00:46:56,880 --> 00:46:58,630
developers before design decisions are

1211
00:46:58,640 --> 00:47:01,349
